          "heading": "Recognize official access categories",
          "body": "The statute separately addresses law enforcement officers conducting official investigations, court orders and SOS direction. Those listed official-access categories permit examination and copying without the ordinary restrictions. Preserve the records and respond through the applicable legal route instead of rewriting entries or destroying material after learning that it has been requested. A notary can preserve a copy of the signed request with the response to show the transaction that was identified and the particular record supplied."
